\ `check` pushes its own pragma frame above the base one the startup file writes to, so a
\ relaxation the user set for themselves reaches the checked program. `check` executes only
\ definition statements, so the guard staying silent is the whole observable: without the startup
\ value both definitions would throw.

dup: ( -- fixnum ) [ 7 ] ;
nip: ( -- fixnum ) [ 9 ] ;
